          "fields": {
            "display_title": "This paper focuses on the continuous transfer learning setting with a time evolving target domain. A major challenge is that the relationship between the source domain and the target domain changes over time. This paper proposes a new C-divergence to measure the discrepancy between domains. It could be utilized to instantiate a tighter error upper bound in the continuous transfer learning setting. The clarity of this paper still needs some improvement. And experimental results are insufficient.",
